    {
      "id": "r20261108-a02",
      "title": "Why More People Are Learning Sign Language",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "In many countries, sign language classes are filling up fast, and most of the students are not deaf. Parents learn to sign with their babies. Nurses learn to help their patients. Baristas learn to take orders from deaf customers.",
        "There are good reasons for this trend. Sign language is a real language with its own grammar, not just hand movements for English words. Learning it opens a door to the deaf community, a group with its own rich culture, jokes, and poetry.",
        "Teachers say the best reason is the simplest one. \"When more people can sign, fewer people are left out,\" says one instructor in Surabaya. \"A short conversation in sign language can turn a lonely day into a friendly one.\""
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "sign language": "bahasa isyarat",
        "deaf": "tuli",
        "filling up": "cepat penuh",
        "patients": "pasien",
        "customers": "pelanggan",
        "trend": "tren",
        "left out": "dikucilkan",
        "instructor": "instruktur"
      },
